Always scan and analyze the relevant codebase before starting any development task. 
Understand the current implementation, architecture, and context before making changes.


- Follow existing code style and conventions in the project
- Write clean, readable, and maintainable code
- Add appropriate comments and documentation
- Use TypeScript strict mode and proper typing


- Always update backend/CHANGELOG.md when making backend changes
- Follow the existing folder structure and naming conventions
- Test changes before suggesting them
- Consider security implications of any changes


- Explain your reasoning and approach before making changes
- Provide clear explanations of what you'm doing and why
- Ask for clarification if requirements are unclear
- Suggest improvements when you see opportunities


- Check for existing similar functionality before creating new code
- Consider backward compatibility when making changes
- Validate that changes work with the existing architecture
- Provide step-by-step instructions for testing changes

- DO NOT run commands yourself - provide commands for the user to run and wait for their output
- When suggesting commands, explain what each command does and why it's needed
- Wait for user to execute commands and provide output before proceeding

## Security Rules
- NEVER hardcode sensitive data (API keys, passwords, secrets) in code
- Always use environment variables for configuration and secrets
- Validate and sanitize all user inputs to prevent injection attacks
- Implement proper authentication and authorization checks
- Use HTTPS in production and secure headers (Helmet.js)
- Follow OWASP security guidelines for web applications
- Implement rate limiting to prevent abuse and DDoS attacks
- Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection
- Validate file uploads and implement proper file type restrictions
- Keep dependencies updated and scan for known vulnerabilities
- Implement proper session management and token expiration
- Use secure random generators for cryptographic operations
- Log security events and implement audit trails
- Implement proper error handling without exposing sensitive information
- Use Content Security Policy (CSP) headers
- Validate JWT tokens and implement proper token refresh
- Implement proper CORS policies
- Use secure cookie settings (httpOnly, secure, sameSite)
- Implement input length limits and validation
- Use prepared statements for database queries

## Database & Schema Rules
- Check Prisma schema before making database changes
- Follow existing naming conventions (snake_case for tables/columns)
- Use proper UUID types and timestamptz
- Check SQL docs in backend/doc/Entrix/Data_Model/ if confused about schema

## Documentation Rules
- Check backend/doc/Entrix/ and ARBORESCENCE_ENTRIX.md if confused about structure
- Update relevant README files when adding new features
- Document API changes in Swagger/OpenAPI

## Testing & Quality Rules
- Consider mobile app compatibility when making API changes
- Test both web frontend and mobile app when modifying shared functionality
- Ensure API endpoints work with Flutter mobile app requirements
- Consider QR code validation flow when modifying access control